<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Every user-facing string in the app.

  Before the redesign all of this was inline English in Kotlin, and `res/values/strings.xml` held
  three entries of which only `app_name` was ever referenced. Nothing else could be translated,
  and nothing could be checked by lint.

  German is not a UI locale here — the app's interface is English, because its users are English
  speakers reading German — but the copy is now externalised, which is the half of localisation
  that has to happen before the other half is possible.
-->
